<h1>Canon Printer Not Connecting to WiFi: Fix It</h1>

<p>A Canon wireless printer makes it easy to print documents, photos, and other files from a computer, laptop, smartphone, or tablet without using a USB cable. However, a common problem users experience is <strong>Canon printer not connecting to WiFi</strong>. The printer may fail to detect the wireless network, reject the WiFi password, disconnect repeatedly, or connect to WiFi but remain unavailable on the computer.</p>

<p>Fortunately, most Canon WiFi connection problems can be resolved by checking the wireless settings, restarting the network, reconnecting the printer, and installing the correct Canon software.</p>

<p>This guide explains <strong>how to connect a Canon printer to WiFi</strong> and provides practical solutions when your Canon printer won't connect to a wireless network.</p>

<h2>Why Is My Canon Printer Not Connecting to WiFi?</h2>

<p>Several things can prevent a Canon printer from connecting to WiFi. Common causes include:</p>

<ul>
<li>Incorrect WiFi password</li>
<li>Weak wireless signal</li>
<li>Printer connected to a different network</li>
<li>Router problems</li>
<li>Unsupported WiFi frequency</li>
<li>Incorrect printer network settings</li>
<li>Outdated or missing Canon drivers</li>
<li>Printer firmware or software problems</li>
<li>Guest WiFi network isolation</li>
<li>VPN or firewall interference</li>
<li>Recently changed router or WiFi password</li>
<li>Temporary communication errors</li>
</ul>

<p>Before making complicated changes, start with the basic connection checks.</p>

<h2>How to Connect a Canon Printer to WiFi</h2>

<p>The exact procedure varies by Canon model, but the general wireless setup process is:</p>

<ol>
<li>Turn on the Canon printer.</li>
<li>Turn on the WiFi router.</li>
<li>Open the printer's wireless/network settings.</li>
<li>Start <strong>Wireless LAN Setup</strong> or a similar option.</li>
<li>Select your WiFi network.</li>
<li>Enter the WiFi password.</li>
<li>Confirm the wireless connection.</li>
<li>Connect your computer to the same WiFi network.</li>
<li>Install the appropriate Canon printer driver.</li>
<li>Add the printer to Windows or macOS.</li>
<li>Print a test page.</li>
</ol>

<p>If your printer has a display, the wireless setup can usually be completed directly from the printer.</p>

<h2>Step 1: Turn On Your Canon Printer</h2>

<p>Connect the printer to a power outlet and press the <strong>Power</strong> button.</p>

<p>Wait until the printer finishes starting up.</p>

<p>Make sure there are no error messages displayed on the printer.</p>

<p>If the printer shows an ink, paper, cartridge, or hardware error, resolve that issue before attempting wireless setup.</p>

<h2>Step 2: Check Your WiFi Router</h2>

<p>Before troubleshooting the printer, verify that your WiFi network is working.</p>

<p>Connect your phone or computer to the same WiFi network and open a website.</p>

<p>If other devices cannot access the internet, restart your router before continuing.</p>

<p>Also make sure the router is within reasonable range of the printer.</p>

<h2>Step 3: Check Your WiFi Name and Password</h2>

<p>Make sure you know the correct:</p>

<ul>
<li>WiFi network name (SSID)</li>
<li>WiFi password</li>
</ul>

<p>When entering the password into the printer, carefully check uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and special characters.</p>

<p>A single incorrect character can prevent the Canon printer from connecting.</p>

<h2>Step 4: Open Wireless Setup on the Canon Printer</h2>

<p>On compatible Canon printers, open the network or wireless settings.</p>

<p>Depending on your model, you may see options such as:</p>

<p><strong>WiFi Setup</strong></p>

<p><strong>Wireless LAN Setup</strong></p>

<p><strong>Wireless Setup</strong></p>

<p><strong>Network Settings</strong></p>

<p>Select the option that starts wireless configuration.</p>

<p>The exact menu names and button combinations vary by Canon printer model.</p>

<h2>Step 5: Select Your WiFi Network</h2>

<p>After starting wireless setup, the printer may search for nearby wireless networks.</p>

<p>Find your home or office WiFi network in the list.</p>

<p>Select the correct network.</p>

<p>If you don't see your network, move the printer closer to the router and search again.</p>

<h2>Step 6: Enter the WiFi Password</h2>

<p>Enter your wireless password when prompted.</p>

<p>Check the password carefully before confirming.</p>

<p>After submitting the password, wait for the printer to establish a connection.</p>

<p>A successful connection may be indicated by a WiFi icon, wireless status message, or network confirmation.</p>

<h2>Step 7: Connect Canon Printer Using WPS</h2>

<p>Some Canon printers support <strong>WPS</strong>, which can simplify wireless setup.</p>

<p>If both your router and printer support WPS:</p>

<ol>
<li>Turn on the Canon printer.</li>
<li>Open the printer's wireless setup menu.</li>
<li>Select WPS.</li>
<li>Press the WPS button on your router when instructed.</li>
<li>Wait for the printer to connect.</li>
<li>Confirm the wireless connection.</li>
</ol>

<p>If WPS doesn't work, use the printer's normal wireless setup method instead.</p>

<h2>How to Connect a Canon Printer to WiFi Using a Computer</h2>

<p>Some Canon printer models can be configured through Canon's setup software.</p>

<p>First, connect your computer to the WiFi network.</p>

<p>Then download the software appropriate for your printer model from <a href="https://www.usa.canon.com/support">Canon Support</a>.</p>

<p>Generally:</p>

<ol>
<li>Search for your exact Canon printer model.</li>
<li>Select your operating system.</li>
<li>Download the recommended setup software or driver.</li>
<li>Open the installer.</li>
<li>Select wireless connection.</li>
<li>Follow the setup instructions.</li>
<li>Allow the software to detect your printer.</li>
<li>Complete the installation.</li>
</ol>

<h2>How to Connect Canon Printer to WiFi on Windows 11</h2>

<p>After the printer has been connected to your wireless network, add it to Windows.</p>

<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Bluetooth &amp; devices</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Printers &amp; scanners</strong>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Add device</strong>.</li>
<li>Wait for Windows to search for available printers.</li>
<li>Select your Canon printer.</li>
<li>Follow the instructions to finish adding it.</li>
</ol>

<p>If Windows cannot find the printer, check that your computer and printer are connected to the same WiFi network.</p>

<h2>How to Connect Canon Printer to WiFi on Windows 10</h2>

<p>For Windows 10:</p>

<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Devices</strong>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Printers &amp; scanners</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Add a printer or scanner</strong>.</li>
<li>Wait for Windows to search.</li>
<li>Select your Canon printer.</li>
<li>Complete the installation.</li>
</ol>

<p>If the printer isn't detected, install the appropriate Canon driver and try again.</p>

<h2>How to Connect Canon Printer to WiFi on Mac</h2>

<p>To add a compatible Canon wireless printer to a Mac:</p>

<ol>
<li>Connect the Mac to your WiFi network.</li>
<li>Connect the Canon printer to the same network.</li>
<li>Open <strong>System Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Printers &amp; Scanners</strong>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Add Printer, Scanner, or Fax</strong>.</li>
<li>Select your Canon printer.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Add</strong>.</li>
<li>Print a test page.</li>
</ol>

<p>For model-specific Canon drivers and software, use <a href="https://www.usa.canon.com/support">Canon Support</a>.</p>

<h2>Canon Printer Not Connecting to WiFi: Top Fixes</h2>

<p>If the wireless setup fails, try the following solutions.</p>

<h3>1. Restart the Canon Printer</h3>

<p>Turn off the printer.</p>

<p>Wait approximately 30 seconds.</p>

<p>Turn it back on and try connecting to WiFi again.</p>

<p>A simple restart can clear temporary network communication problems.</p>

<h3>2. Restart Your WiFi Router</h3>

<p>Turn off your router.</p>

<p>Wait for about 30 seconds.</p>

<p>Turn it back on and allow it to reconnect to the internet.</p>

<p>Then try connecting your Canon printer again.</p>

<h3>3. Verify the WiFi Password</h3>

<p>Incorrect passwords are one of the simplest reasons a printer won't connect.</p>

<p>Check your password carefully and make sure you aren't accidentally entering the password for another network.</p>

<h3>4. Move the Printer Closer to the Router</h3>

<p>A weak WiFi signal can cause connection failures.</p>

<p>For initial setup, place the Canon printer closer to the router.</p>

<p>After the connection works, you can move the printer to its normal location.</p>

<h3>5. Check 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz Compatibility</h3>

<p>Some Canon printer models support 2.4 GHz wireless networks but may not support 5 GHz networks.</p>

<p>If your router provides separate networks, try connecting the printer to the supported 2.4 GHz network.</p>

<p>If your router combines 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz under one network name, check the router and printer documentation for compatibility.</p>

<h3>6. Don't Use a Guest Network</h3>

<p>Guest networks can isolate connected devices.</p>

<p>For example:</p>

<p><strong>Computer:</strong> HomeWiFi</p>

<p><strong>Printer:</strong> HomeWiFi-Guest</p>

<p>The printer may have internet access but still be inaccessible from the computer.</p>

<p>Connect the printer and computer to the same primary network whenever possible.</p>

<h3>7. Check the Printer's WiFi Indicator</h3>

<p>Look at the printer's WiFi icon or network status.</p>

<p>If the wireless indicator is off, the printer may not be connected.</p>

<p>If it repeatedly flashes or shows an error, open the network settings and perform wireless setup again.</p>

<h3>8. Reset the Canon Printer's Network Settings</h3>

<p>If the printer previously connected to another router or WiFi network, old network information may interfere with setup.</p>

<p>Reset the printer's network settings according to your model's instructions.</p>

<p>Then:</p>

<ol>
<li>Start wireless setup again.</li>
<li>Select your current WiFi network.</li>
<li>Enter the current password.</li>
<li>Confirm the connection.</li>
<li>Add the printer to your computer again.</li>
</ol>

<p>The exact network-reset procedure varies by Canon model.</p>

<h2>Canon Printer Connected to WiFi but Computer Can't Find It</h2>

<p>Sometimes the printer successfully connects to WiFi but doesn't appear on the computer.</p>

<p>Try these solutions:</p>

<h3>Check the Networks</h3>

<p>Make sure the printer and computer are connected to the same local network.</p>

<h3>Restart Both Devices</h3>

<p>Restart the printer and computer.</p>

<h3>Check the Firewall</h3>

<p>Windows Firewall or third-party security software can sometimes interfere with local printer discovery.</p>

<h3>Disconnect VPN</h3>

<p>A VPN can interfere with communication between your computer and devices on your local network.</p>

<p>Temporarily disconnect the VPN and check whether the printer appears.</p>

<h3>Reinstall the Driver</h3>

<p>Download and install the appropriate Canon printer driver for your exact model.</p>

<h2>Canon Printer Connected to WiFi but Not Printing</h2>

<p>A WiFi connection doesn't guarantee that printing will work.</p>

<p>Check the following:</p>

<ul>
<li>Printer is powered on</li>
<li>Paper is loaded</li>
<li>Ink is available</li>
<li>Printer isn't displaying an error</li>
<li>Print queue isn't stuck</li>
<li>Correct printer is selected</li>
<li>Printer isn't offline</li>
<li>Correct driver is installed</li>
<li>Computer and printer are on the same network</li>
</ul>

<p>Try printing a simple document after checking these items.</p>

<h2>Canon Printer Keeps Disconnecting From WiFi</h2>

<p>If the printer connects but repeatedly loses the wireless connection, try these steps:</p>

<ol>
<li>Move the printer closer to the router.</li>
<li>Restart the router.</li>
<li>Restart the printer.</li>
<li>Check WiFi signal strength.</li>
<li>Check whether the printer supports your wireless frequency.</li>
<li>Avoid guest WiFi.</li>
<li>Check router device-isolation settings.</li>
<li>Update compatible Canon software or firmware.</li>
<li>Reconfigure the printer's wireless connection.</li>
</ol>

<p>If other devices also lose their WiFi connection, the problem may be with the router rather than the printer.</p>

<h2>Canon Printer Won't Connect After Changing WiFi Password</h2>

<p>If you recently changed your WiFi password, your Canon printer may still have the old password stored.</p>

<p>You'll need to reconnect it.</p>

<h3>Steps</h3>

<ol>
<li>Open the printer's wireless settings.</li>
<li>Start wireless setup.</li>
<li>Select the current WiFi network.</li>
<li>Enter the new password.</li>
<li>Confirm the connection.</li>
<li>Wait for the printer to connect.</li>
<li>Check the printer from your computer.</li>
</ol>

<p>If the printer continues to fail, reset its network settings and configure WiFi again.</p>

<h2>Canon Printer Won't Connect After Getting a New Router</h2>

<p>A new router may have a different network name and password.</p>

<p>To reconnect:</p>

<ol>
