<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Why is my Canon printer not connecting to WiFi?</h3>

<p>The most common causes are an incorrect WiFi password, weak signal, unsupported wireless frequency, router problems, incorrect network settings, or a problem with the printer's wireless configuration.</p>

<h3>How do I connect my Canon printer to WiFi?</h3>

<p>Open the printer's wireless settings, select your WiFi network, enter the password, and confirm the connection. Then add the printer to your computer through Windows or macOS.</p>

<h3>How do I connect a Canon printer to WiFi without WPS?</h3>

<p>Use the printer's <strong>Wireless LAN Setup</strong> or <strong>WiFi Setup</strong> option. Select your network, enter the password, and confirm the connection.</p>

<h3>Why can't my Canon printer find my WiFi?</h3>

<p>Restart your router, move the printer closer to it, check whether the network is visible, and verify that your printer supports the router's wireless frequency.</p>

<h3>Why is my Canon printer connected to WiFi but offline?</h3>

<p>The computer may be connected to a different network, the printer driver may be incorrect, or Windows may have marked the printer offline. Restart both devices and verify the network and printer settings.</p>

<h3>Why does my Canon printer keep disconnecting from WiFi?</h3>

<p>Weak signal strength, router issues, wireless interference, incompatible network settings, or unsupported WiFi bands can cause repeated disconnections.</p>

<h3>Can I connect my Canon printer to 5 GHz WiFi?</h3>

<p>It depends on the printer model. Some Canon printers support 2.4 GHz only, while other models support additional wireless configurations. Check the specifications for your exact model.</p>

<h3>How do I reconnect my Canon printer after changing the WiFi password?</h3>

<p>Open the printer's wireless settings, select your current WiFi network, enter the new password, and complete the connection. If necessary, reset the printer's network settings first.</p>

<h3>How do I connect my Canon printer to a laptop?</h3>

<p>First connect the printer to WiFi. Then connect the laptop to the same network and install the appropriate Canon driver. Add the printer through Windows or macOS printer settings.</p>

<h3>Can I connect my Canon printer to WiFi using my phone?</h3>

<p>Some compatible Canon printers support wireless setup and mobile printing through Canon's mobile applications or supported mobile printing features. The exact process depends on the model.</p>

<h2>Conclusion</h2>

<p>When your <strong>Canon printer is not connecting to WiFi</strong>, the problem is often related to the wireless network, password, printer configuration, signal strength, or computer connection. Start by restarting the printer and router, checking the WiFi password, and making sure the printer and computer are connected to the same network.</p>

<p>To <strong>connect a Canon printer to WiFi</strong>, open the printer's wireless setup menu, select your network, enter the correct password, and wait for the connection to complete. If your printer and router support WPS, you can also use the WPS method.</p>

<p>If the printer connects to WiFi but your computer cannot find it, install the correct Canon driver, check firewall and VPN settings, and make sure both devices are on the same local network. For model-specific drivers, software, manuals, and setup information, use <a href="https://www.usa.canon.com/support">Canon Support</a>.</p>

<p>With the correct wireless settings and compatible Canon software, most Canon WiFi connection problems can be resolved without needing a USB connection.</p>

